WEBVTT

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:08.600
Wh-Who are you...

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:10.400
I'll just tell you.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:11.620
It's Megumu-san.

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:12.900
Trip.

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:15.660
Why did you tell him, Ruri-chan?!

00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:18.960
I thought it'd be better if 
we didn't let this drag out.

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:22.410
Megumu, why are you...

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:26.420
My sisters came and are staying nearby,

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:29.680
so they snuck into our place and

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:32.020
switched all my clothes for girls clothes...

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:33.800
Oh, I see.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:37.050
Well, I'm sorry for worrying you, anyway.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:40.560
No, I'm glad you're okay.

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:53.370
<b>If Her Flag Breaks</b>

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:16.990
<b>Flag 7</b>

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:16.990
<b>I Learned Something Amazing. I'll Hide Myself Before I can be Erased</b>

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:19.780
So you agreed to be brother and sister...

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:21.130
That's right.

00:02:21.130 --> 00:02:24.480
I'm now Souta-oniichan's little sister.

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:26.790
That's nice!

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:28.470
Little sisters are nice!

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:30.040
I want one, too!

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:32.480
What are you doing?

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:33.740
No!

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:37.550
It's a bad thing to care more about 
little sisters than older ones!

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:41.330
You like little sisters better?!

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:43.310
You traitor!

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:43.800
Hey, Okiku-nee, calm down!

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:45.370
Indeed.

00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:47.630
If you wanted a little sister that badly,

00:02:47.630 --> 00:02:49.200
why not just be with

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:51.830
your little android sister right here.

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:55.070
Not you, too, Ruri-chan!

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:56.940
Don't make things worse!

00:02:57.690 --> 00:02:59.190
I'm sorry.

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:03.200
It doesn't really matter how 
happy I am to have a brother if

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:06.640
I'm just going to hurt his 
older sister in the process...

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:08.330
If you're my brother's little sister,

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:10.420
then you're his older sister's little sister.

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:12.030
That's why I need to be 
the older sister here,

00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:14.390
and recognize you as the little 
sister of my younger brother.

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:17.730
Hug, hug, hug.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.890
So I'd like to take Kurumiko back with

00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:22.190
us to Hatagaya Academy, if possible.

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:25.570
Well, let's see...

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:28.220
Little Souta's asking.

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:30.600
Do something for us, Little Mimori.

00:03:30.830 --> 00:03:32.860
I'm not taking no for an answer.

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:35.110
When did you start spoiling him?!

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:37.780
Please, President...

00:03:38.210 --> 00:03:39.640
Hatate-kun...

00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:44.410
She's the chairwoman's granddaughter, 
so she's always pulling a lot of stuff,

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:46.580
but that sometimes comes in handy.

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:48.290
Yeah, but...

00:03:48.590 --> 00:03:51.840
Sorry for introducing myself so late.

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:54.660
Here's a present for you.

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:56.130
Thank you.

00:03:58.930 --> 00:04:00.390
What? This doesn't taste like anything!

00:04:00.710 --> 00:04:03.760
Well, I guess we'll have to 
use "give and take" here.

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:07.350
Hm... As compensation, how about 
during tomorrow's free period,

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:10.020
Souta goes on a date with you?

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:11.740
A-A date?!

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:14.020
Now you're just making light of me.

00:04:14.450 --> 00:04:18.020
A date with Seiteikouji 
Mimori doesn't come cheap!

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:21.410
Guess you'll just have 
to buy her a juice box.

00:04:21.410 --> 00:04:22.990
A date with me's worth less than a juice box?!

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:25.700
A date'll be fine. I want the date.

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:28.430
I've kind of wanted some 
good summer memories.

00:04:28.430 --> 00:04:29.990
Guess it's settled, then.

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:31.330
Huh? Wait...

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:32.560
Um...

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:34.240
Come on...

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:37.060
If you fall in love with me, 
Hatate, it's not my fault.

00:04:45.190 --> 00:04:46.940
Roar! Gawo!

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:49.760
What's wrong?

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:51.850
You know it's not like I'm really

00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:54.560
excited because it's our first date.

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:56.500
Oh, right.

00:04:56.500 --> 00:04:57.520
That's fine.

00:04:57.520 --> 00:04:59.250
R-Really?

00:04:59.550 --> 00:05:01.610
Okay, let's go.

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:04.400
There's a beautiful stream 
deep in the forest.

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:05.900
Oh, right.

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:15.830
That's cold!

00:05:17.030 --> 00:05:18.220
<i>It's kind of nice to be</i>

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:21.300
<i>with a girl whose flag I 
can't get in an instant.</i>

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:27.070
I'm boring, aren't I?

00:05:27.070 --> 00:05:27.920
Huh?

00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:30.040
Don't worry about it.

00:05:30.040 --> 00:05:31.550
I know myself.

00:05:31.550 --> 00:05:34.080
No normal guy would want

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:36.000
to go on a date with me.

00:05:37.150 --> 00:05:40.360
Sorry for making you spend time with me.

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:44.550
I'll do what I can for Kurumiko-kun.

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:47.640
I don't really dislike you or anything.

00:05:49.010 --> 00:05:50.680
You're kind.

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:54.040
I'm a loud person.

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:56.750
I know I'm not really that girly.

00:05:57.480 --> 00:06:00.800
But I can't stop being who I am,

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:01.930
nor do I want to.

00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:06.400
That's because I'm Seiteikouji Mimori.

00:06:09.190 --> 00:06:10.640
Is something wrong?

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:12.270
It feels like

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:15.280
you're living earnestly, unlike me.

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:16.560
Hm?

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:19.650
You might cause a lot of ruckus,

00:06:19.650 --> 00:06:22.250
but you're just enjoying life.

00:06:22.660 --> 00:06:25.960
You really stand out to me, 
since I've given up on everything.

00:06:31.070 --> 00:06:32.160
Mimori,

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:34.350
I'm envious of you.

00:06:34.350 --> 00:06:35.760
You shouldn't be.

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:38.790
I mean, everyone thinks you're 
far better than I am.

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:42.280
You might always be causing trouble,

00:06:42.280 --> 00:06:45.800
but that means you're living life to the 
fullest, standing out to everyone.

00:06:46.690 --> 00:06:50.340
That's why you should stay the way you are.

00:06:55.110 --> 00:06:57.310
But I wonder if

00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:00.070
I'm really here,

00:07:00.470 --> 00:07:04.320
if I'm really living.

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:13.120
You're at the center of everyone.

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:15.070
That's something to be proud of,

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:18.620
and I'm sure everyone loves you.

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:21.870
That's what it means to be alive, isn't it?

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:28.880
Don't make that face.

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:30.260
You're alive, too.

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:33.020
Everyone alive must become happy.

00:07:35.340 --> 00:07:37.270
Hatate-kun, I'll...

00:07:37.270 --> 00:07:39.770
I'll make you happy.

00:07:42.880 --> 00:07:44.980
<i>Is this a flag, too?</i>

00:07:52.010 --> 00:07:52.930
I...

00:07:53.580 --> 00:07:57.580
I'll do what I can to help you.

00:07:57.990 --> 00:08:01.000
I mean... You can depend on me. Yeah.

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:03.630
If everyone turns against you,

00:08:03.630 --> 00:08:07.170
I'll be there for you, Souta-kun.

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:10.510
I'm sorry. I called you by your name.

00:08:10.510 --> 00:08:12.760
It's fine. I don't really mind.

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:14.040
Really?!

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:15.560
I mean, really?

00:08:15.560 --> 00:08:17.010
Cool.

00:08:17.450 --> 00:08:19.730
Souta-kun. Souta-kun.

00:08:21.930 --> 00:08:24.050
I'll take care of Kurumiko-kun, okay?

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:26.300
I'll...

00:08:26.600 --> 00:08:28.650
I'll do what I can for you.

00:08:38.840 --> 00:08:42.330
Okay, everyone, get on the bus.

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:44.920
Stay in line and don't fight.

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:47.520
I see...

00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:48.600
I'm sorry.

00:08:48.950 --> 00:08:52.270
I told you to come, and then...

00:08:52.270 --> 00:08:54.080
Hatate-kun isn't the one at fault.

00:08:54.080 --> 00:08:57.950
I wasn't able to do anything...

00:08:59.340 --> 00:09:02.890
I'm sad I'll have to be away from you,

00:09:03.240 --> 00:09:05.950
but our hearts will be together.

00:09:05.950 --> 00:09:07.460
Right?

00:09:08.530 --> 00:09:10.400
Yeah.

00:09:10.620 --> 00:09:13.570
I'm glad we were just able to meet

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:17.530
and become brother and sister.

00:09:18.470 --> 00:09:19.570
Kurumiko...

00:09:29.180 --> 00:09:32.150
Souta-kun, the beach was fun, wasn't it?

00:09:32.450 --> 00:09:33.920
Y-Yeah.

00:09:34.220 --> 00:09:36.120
I guess so.

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:38.970
I want to go again with you.

00:09:39.190 --> 00:09:41.190
If Souta's going, I'm going, too.

00:09:41.190 --> 00:09:41.990
Me, too.

00:09:41.990 --> 00:09:42.890
Me, too.

00:09:42.890 --> 00:09:46.730
W-Well, if everyone's going, 
I guess I'll go, too.

00:09:48.040 --> 00:09:49.000
Yeah.

00:09:49.300 --> 00:09:52.010
I guess we can go if we 
don't have to go to the sea.

00:09:52.010 --> 00:09:54.230
What does that mean?

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:57.240
Welcome back.

00:09:57.490 --> 00:09:59.730
Huh? Kurumiko?

00:09:59.730 --> 00:10:01.080
Why are you here?

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:04.650
A nice girl brought me.

00:10:08.630 --> 00:10:10.080
Hello there.

00:10:12.010 --> 00:10:14.340
Daimyouzamurai Mei.

00:10:24.250 --> 00:10:25.890
What's going on?

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:28.450
I just altered the

00:10:28.450 --> 00:10:30.570
school's data, that's all.

00:10:30.870 --> 00:10:32.390
I didn't think of that!

00:10:32.390 --> 00:10:34.900
You're useless when it matters.

00:10:35.140 --> 00:10:36.450
I did my best!

00:10:36.450 --> 00:10:37.650
How mean!

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:42.010
So why are the student council 
president and Granny here?

00:10:42.010 --> 00:10:46.000
That's because we're going to 
live here at Quest Dorm, too.

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:48.440
We already completed the paperwork.

00:10:48.440 --> 00:10:49.160
What was that?!

00:10:50.220 --> 00:10:51.920
Are you trying to get me to
owe you a favor?

00:10:52.800 --> 00:10:53.840
Not really.

00:10:54.130 --> 00:10:57.840
I just didn't like what was 
happening, is all.

00:10:57.840 --> 00:10:58.680
Huh?

00:10:58.980 --> 00:11:00.840
I'm glad everyone's here.

00:11:01.320 --> 00:11:03.570
Kurumiko-chan, the 
student council president,

00:11:03.570 --> 00:11:07.370
Granny, and Mei! All four 
of you are moving in!

00:11:07.370 --> 00:11:09.100
Why me?

00:11:09.100 --> 00:11:12.600
I have no plans on getting 
friendly with you all.

00:11:12.940 --> 00:11:14.450
Are you leaving?

00:11:14.450 --> 00:11:16.620
I'd like it if a nice girl

00:11:16.620 --> 00:11:19.120
like you was around...

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:26.290
I'll live here, too.

00:11:26.290 --> 00:11:29.190
Okay, then let's sleep together tonight.

00:11:29.190 --> 00:11:30.960
Wait. Why?

00:11:31.180 --> 00:11:34.940
I won't be able to sleep by myself.

00:11:35.240 --> 00:11:38.180
Just ask Hatate Souta for—

00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:41.460
Fine. Just today.

00:11:42.340 --> 00:11:44.420
She doesn't look it, but she was easy.

00:11:48.520 --> 00:11:51.420
Okay, I'm off.

00:12:02.860 --> 00:12:05.510
Tell me, Daimyouzamurai... You—

00:12:05.510 --> 00:12:06.700
Call me Mei.

00:12:07.030 --> 00:12:10.000
You can see flags, right?

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:12.170
Yes, but my power is

00:12:12.170 --> 00:12:14.960
artificial and limited.

00:12:15.820 --> 00:12:17.620
However, you're different.

00:12:18.220 --> 00:12:20.240
The ability to alter flags...

00:12:20.640 --> 00:12:24.220
You were given that power by the sacraments.

00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:25.700
Sacrament?

00:12:26.070 --> 00:12:27.370
You mean Sakura?

00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:30.310
It's something which a human would

00:12:30.310 --> 00:12:33.110
normally never be able to possess.

00:12:33.110 --> 00:12:36.940
A power which allows one 
to alter fate itself.

00:12:37.710 --> 00:12:38.980
The Angel Boat.

00:12:40.200 --> 00:12:40.990
What's that?

00:12:41.620 --> 00:12:43.850
It travels all water in existence,

00:12:43.850 --> 00:12:47.240
a boat of fate capable of 
controlling all there is.

00:12:48.030 --> 00:12:51.330
You have a power on that level, Hatate Souta,

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:53.470
and what do you wish to do with it?

00:12:56.540 --> 00:13:00.490
First, I'd like to rid 
myself of this death flag.

00:13:01.570 --> 00:13:03.580
First?

00:13:03.580 --> 00:13:04.460
Yes.

00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:06.670
The second is a request from Sakura,

00:13:06.970 --> 00:13:08.010
I guess.

00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:11.060
I will give you my power.

00:13:11.450 --> 00:13:13.430
And in exchange,

00:13:13.430 --> 00:13:16.560
you must learn the ultimate 
truth of this world.

00:13:17.080 --> 00:13:18.760
The ultimate truth of this world?

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:20.060
I see.

00:13:20.060 --> 00:13:21.670
So that's it.

00:13:22.620 --> 00:13:23.820
Huh? You know something?

00:13:24.360 --> 00:13:27.090
Those who seek will find happiness,

00:13:27.090 --> 00:13:29.740
for you learn the most when you 
realize how little you know.

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:31.330
Very well.

00:13:34.840 --> 00:13:37.050
Phase shift, clear.

00:13:37.820 --> 00:13:40.000
Spacial link, clear.

00:13:40.320 --> 00:13:42.530
Gate release.

00:13:43.360 --> 00:13:45.080
I'll shall show you

00:13:45.080 --> 00:13:47.820
part of the truth of this world.

00:13:52.270 --> 00:13:53.360
We didn't go anywhere?

00:13:54.040 --> 00:13:55.910
Hey, wait. Mei!

00:13:57.730 --> 00:14:00.600
We're in the Hatagaya 
Academy building, right?

00:14:00.960 --> 00:14:02.670
What are you trying to do?

00:14:02.670 --> 00:14:04.070
You'll understand soon.

00:14:07.790 --> 00:14:08.930
S-Sorry.

00:14:09.750 --> 00:14:10.620
Okiku-nee?

00:14:11.370 --> 00:14:12.800
What's up with you?

00:14:12.800 --> 00:14:15.960
Another first year trying to 
do something to Kikuno?

00:14:15.960 --> 00:14:17.570
R-Rin-kun...

00:14:17.570 --> 00:14:19.110
How dare you?

00:14:19.110 --> 00:14:21.830
I never said you could call me by my name.

00:14:21.830 --> 00:14:24.060
<i>Huh? What's going on?</i>

00:14:25.190 --> 00:14:27.030
Sorry about my friend.

00:14:27.030 --> 00:14:29.340
It seems we mistook you for someone else.

00:14:29.640 --> 00:14:30.590
I see.

00:14:30.590 --> 00:14:32.230
Be careful.

00:14:34.940 --> 00:14:37.410
It seems the girls in this world

00:14:37.410 --> 00:14:39.560
don't know you.

00:14:39.560 --> 00:14:41.470
This world...

00:14:42.710 --> 00:14:45.280
In order to put it into 
something you'd understand...

00:14:45.700 --> 00:14:48.530
We're on an Earth from a parallel universe.

00:14:49.320 --> 00:14:50.650
Parallel universe?

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:54.540
The Council of the Seven 
Virtues watches the worlds.

00:14:54.840 --> 00:14:55.910
The Council of the Seven Virtues?

00:14:56.350 --> 00:14:59.110
Right now we're currently watching

00:14:59.110 --> 00:15:03.110
the Sacraments and you, 
Hatate Souta, the closest.

00:15:03.660 --> 00:15:06.290
It is my job to figure out if

00:15:06.290 --> 00:15:08.730
you will bring harm to the worlds.

00:15:08.730 --> 00:15:10.430
I couldn't...

00:15:11.180 --> 00:15:16.080
Your power is far greater than you realize.

00:15:20.190 --> 00:15:21.200
We're...

00:15:28.170 --> 00:15:29.110
Nanami...

00:16:11.460 --> 00:16:12.610
No...

00:16:13.390 --> 00:16:14.570
This is...

00:16:15.170 --> 00:16:17.580
We're on the Premium Ambriel...

00:16:28.170 --> 00:16:30.200
<i>I... I see.</i>

00:16:30.500 --> 00:16:32.080
<i>In this world, I...</i>

00:16:34.330 --> 00:16:35.810
You're not going to run?

00:16:36.520 --> 00:16:37.820
Everyone died.

00:16:38.120 --> 00:16:40.840
If I'm going to be alone, 
then I might as well...

00:16:43.420 --> 00:16:45.190
Wh-What are you doing?

00:16:45.840 --> 00:16:47.500
You might think it's

00:16:47.820 --> 00:16:50.690
better to die here, but...

00:16:51.450 --> 00:16:52.500
Then...

00:16:53.950 --> 00:16:55.630
I still want you to live.

00:16:55.960 --> 00:16:57.910
You will meet people.

00:16:58.950 --> 00:17:02.560
People who will be happy you lived.

00:17:05.020 --> 00:17:06.390
Just like I

00:17:07.130 --> 00:17:09.270
met everyone at Quest Dorm.

00:17:09.570 --> 00:17:10.170
Huh?

00:17:15.520 --> 00:17:16.810
M-Miyuki-sensei?

00:17:20.650 --> 00:17:24.740
I didn't think I'd hear about Quest Dorm here.

00:17:25.040 --> 00:17:25.690
Huh?

00:17:25.910 --> 00:17:28.420
Just a little before the Second World War,

00:17:28.420 --> 00:17:32.110
my great grandfather went 
missing underground there.

00:17:33.230 --> 00:17:34.840
Under Quest Dorm?

00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:37.250
Could that be...

00:17:39.320 --> 00:17:41.710
Sorry, who's you great grandfather?

00:17:42.740 --> 00:17:45.210
I think his name was Hatate Souta.

00:17:46.740 --> 00:17:50.230
I forgot to mention it, 
but my name is Hatate Miyuki.

00:17:52.580 --> 00:17:53.570
Crap.

00:17:53.570 --> 00:17:54.260
Miyuki-san!

00:17:54.660 --> 00:17:56.170
I'm fine.

00:17:56.520 --> 00:18:00.510
I have a reason to live now!

00:18:05.240 --> 00:18:08.090
<i>That's the main character flag...</i>

00:18:08.840 --> 00:18:11.330
Your words have given me power,

00:18:11.630 --> 00:18:14.400
and I just like you, I...

00:18:18.780 --> 00:18:19.830
Where am I...

00:18:20.270 --> 00:18:22.280
This is the world you started in.

00:18:22.540 --> 00:18:23.600
I see.

00:18:24.410 --> 00:18:25.790
I'm back...

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:30.200
That world will revolve 
around Miyuki MacKenzie, no,

00:18:30.200 --> 00:18:33.430
Hatate Miyuki.

00:18:33.430 --> 00:18:35.800
That's right, as the main character.

00:18:35.800 --> 00:18:37.620
You have an enormous power,

00:18:37.620 --> 00:18:40.430
capable of altering they 
very core of a world.

00:18:40.730 --> 00:18:43.890
And using that power, you...

00:18:43.890 --> 00:18:46.310
Huh? Is something wrong?

00:18:46.310 --> 00:18:48.440
You look pale.

00:18:48.740 --> 00:18:49.670
I'm fine.

00:18:49.970 --> 00:18:51.610
I'll be fine, after I rest a little.

00:18:55.760 --> 00:18:56.660
Huh?

00:18:57.470 --> 00:19:01.160
I finally got closer to the ultimate 
truth of the world, and I...

00:19:04.050 --> 00:19:04.840
Wait...

00:19:04.840 --> 00:19:07.440
Is the activated death flag in 
you making you say all of that?

00:19:07.440 --> 00:19:08.750
At this rate, he's going to...

00:19:09.950 --> 00:19:11.170
I guess I'll have to do it!

00:19:17.610 --> 00:19:19.450
<i>This is death...</i>

00:19:19.750 --> 00:19:21.050
<i>This is fear!</i>

00:19:21.430 --> 00:19:24.310
<i>The truth behind the power to change flags.</i>

00:19:24.310 --> 00:19:28.060
<i>You must bear all the fate in the world by yourself.</i>

00:19:28.320 --> 00:19:30.660
<i>What despair!</i>

00:19:30.660 --> 00:19:31.440
<i>I'm afraid!</i>

00:19:31.440 --> 00:19:32.790
<i>Afraid! Afraid!</i>

00:19:32.790 --> 00:19:36.060
<i>But he's born this burden for so long...</i>

00:19:36.060 --> 00:19:37.400
I won't let him die!

00:19:37.400 --> 00:19:39.020
This person will save

00:19:39.020 --> 00:19:41.570
<i>the Council of the Seven Virtues, and the world!</i>

00:19:41.570 --> 00:19:43.570
Please! Mother! Father!

00:19:43.800 --> 00:19:47.220
Everyone! Help me!

00:19:58.200 --> 00:20:01.390
I've only delayed its activation temporarily.

00:20:02.810 --> 00:20:06.940
You're so weak, so naïve, but

00:20:07.650 --> 00:20:10.770
I'm so proud I saved you.

00:20:11.660 --> 00:20:15.080
I didn't know your warmth 
could be so endearing.

00:20:23.780 --> 00:20:25.030
The Sacraments!

00:20:25.460 --> 00:20:27.030
I'm sorry.

00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:30.680
I can't have you doing all of this.

00:20:31.070 --> 00:20:35.250
The apostles of the seven virtues 
know too many things

00:20:35.250 --> 00:20:36.870
that he can't be allowed to know.

00:20:40.830 --> 00:20:42.640
I'm sorry. I really am.

00:20:42.960 --> 00:20:46.840
He will find the ultimate truth

00:20:46.840 --> 00:20:48.580
of the world on his own.

00:20:54.140 --> 00:20:56.560
Hm? Are you awake?

00:20:56.790 --> 00:20:57.690
Mei?

00:20:58.130 --> 00:21:00.570
Wait. Why are you...

00:21:00.570 --> 00:21:02.280
I don't know...

00:21:02.280 --> 00:21:04.500
The next thing I knew I was...

00:21:04.500 --> 00:21:05.700
What are you...

00:21:06.280 --> 00:21:07.830
Complete

00:21:08.240 --> 00:21:09.700
The conquest completed flag?

00:21:09.920 --> 00:21:12.170
What are you saying?

00:21:12.170 --> 00:21:14.490
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:21:14.490 --> 00:21:16.340
Mei, can you see flags?

00:21:16.340 --> 00:21:18.210
What about the Council of the Seven Virtues?

00:21:18.740 --> 00:21:21.710
Flags? The Council of the Seven Virtues?

00:21:23.210 --> 00:21:24.510
<i>Her memory's</i>

00:21:25.770 --> 00:21:26.710
<i>gone?</i>

00:23:11.060 --> 00:23:12.390
Roar! Gawo!

00:23:12.390 --> 00:23:14.680
You're half-Japanese, right, Miyuki-sensei?

00:23:14.680 --> 00:23:16.430
It turns out I am.

00:23:16.430 --> 00:23:18.520
I'm not sure why you said 
"it turns out," but whatever.

00:23:18.520 --> 00:23:19.960
There's a big difference between you and me,

00:23:19.960 --> 00:23:21.680
even though we're both half-Japanese.

00:23:22.130 --> 00:23:25.390
I'm sure your boobs will get bigger.

00:23:25.390 --> 00:23:26.720
I was talking about our height!

00:23:26.720 --> 00:23:31.180
Kids grow fast, so I'm sure you'll look 
different by the start of summer break.

00:23:31.180 --> 00:23:33.670
That's the "I'm totally 
not getting bigger" flag!

00:23:31.760 --> 00:23:35.010
<b>Flag 8</b>

00:23:31.760 --> 00:23:35.010
<b>I'll catch up to you. Have I ever broken a promise to you before?{Z: you'll probably have to adjust font size depending on length of translation.}</b>

00:23:33.670 --> 00:23:35.010
Roar! Gawo!

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>If Her Flag Breaks</b>

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>Hope you watch next time.</b>

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.020
Illustration: Mizu Asato
